# 📚 Book REST API

A simple, educational REST API for managing books built with **Node.js** and **Express.js**.

## Prerequisites

- Node.js 18+ installed
- npm (comes with Node.js)

## Installation

```bash
# Clone or navigate to the project directory
cd book-rest-api

# Install dependencies
npm install
```

## Running the API

### Development mode (with auto-restart on file changes):
```bash
npm run dev
```

### Production mode:
```bash
npm start
```

The server starts at **http://localhost:3000** by default. Set the `PORT` environment variable to change it:
```bash
PORT=8080 npm start
```

## API Endpoints

| Method | Endpoint          | Description              |
|--------|-------------------|--------------------------|
| GET    | `/`               | API info & endpoint list |
| GET    | `/books`          | List all books (with filtering) |
| GET    | `/books/:id`      | Get a single book by ID  |
| POST   | `/books`          | Create a new book        |
| PUT    | `/books/:id`      | Update an existing book  |
| DELETE | `/books/:id`      | Delete a book            |
| GET    | `/stats`          | Get collection statistics|

## Testing with curl

### Get API info
```bash
curl http://localhost:3000/
```

### List all books
```bash
curl http://localhost:3000/books
```

### List books filtered by genre
```bash
curl "http://localhost:3000/books?genre=Fiction"
```

### List books published between two years
```bash
curl "http://localhost:3000/books?minYear=1950&maxYear=2000"
```

### Get a single book
```bash
curl http://localhost:3000/books/1
```

### Create a new book
```bash
curl -X POST http://localhost:3000/books \
  -H "Content-Type: application/json" \
  -d '{
    "title": "1984",
    "author": "George Orwell",
    "isbn": "978-0451524935",
