## Summary of Key Patterns Used

| Pattern | Where Applied | Why |
|---|---|---|
| **Custom Error Classes** | `src/errors/CustomError.js` | Structured errors with status codes; distinguishes operational vs programmer errors |
| **Global Error Handler** | `src/middleware/errorHandler.js` | Single place for error formatting; catches async errors automatically |
| **Validation Middleware** | `src/middleware/validator.js` | Separates input checking from route logic; reusable across routes |
| **Data Abstraction Layer** | `src/data/books.js` | Routes don't know about storage — swap array for DB later without changing routes |
| **Express Router** | `src/routes/books.js`, `stats.js` | Modular route organization; clean mounting at `/books` and `/stats` |
| **Async/Await + try/catch** | Route handlers | Readable async code; explicit error propagation via `next(err)` |
| **Consistent Response Format** | All routes | `{ success, data }` or `{ success, error }` — clients know what to expect |
| **404 Catch-All** | `src/index.js` | JSON-formatted 404s instead of Express's default HTML |

